extends RefCounted
## Local voices for each city: what the passengers are called, what they
## shout, how they review you, and how they walk out. riders.gd falls back to
## the general lines for anything a city doesn't override.
##
## Tone rules: affectionate, everyday local expressions, said in English with
## a local word or two. No mocking accents or spellings, nothing religious,
## no real businesses, people or tragedies.
##
## Per city, per passenger type:
##   label    the type's local nickname (Nana is "Nonna" in Rome)
##   names    local first names
##   says     moment -> lines (pickup, crash, jump, near, splash, slow, fast, drift)
##   reviews  stars (1 or 5) -> lines
##   bail     walk-out lines

